    "description": "Product Description Save over $150.00 off the combined price of buying the stones individually. This handy kit contains one each of the Ruby Stones listed in the TechSpec. Ruby Stones are the ideal choice for deburring, blending, dressing, and fine polishing of molds & dies made of hard metals such as hardened tool steel, carbide and surgical stainless steel. Jewelers use them for sharpening of carbide and high-speed steel engravers and other tools. Mold & Die Uses: Deburring ejector pin holes. General deburring and edge breaking on mold steel and carbide. Blending a surface where a straight edge meets a radius. Polishing highly detailed areas on dies (after dressing Ruby Stone to a fine point). Ruby Midget Files can be used in an Ultrasonic Handpiece for fast deburring and blending in ribs and other hard to reach areas. Ruby Stones cut faster than our very popular Super Ceramic Stones. Medical Instruments: Fine polishing of surgical stainless-steel instruments. Jewelers and Engravers: Polishing and shaping of carbide & high-speed steel gravers. Made in Germany from pure, sintered crystals of synthetic ruby. No bonding material is used, so these stones and files are extremely hard and resistant to changes in shape. This is particularly important for quality precision grinding and finishing. In addition, since Degussit Ruby Stones and Files feature outstanding resistance to wear, they are more economical to use than other comparable tools. Use dry or with Gesswein Stoning Oil to grind, touch up or debur steel and carbide parts. Also recommended for use on materials such as glass, quartz and porcelain. *All dimensions have a tolerance of ±0.1mm. Show More Product Specifications Brand: DEGUSSIT® Abrasive: Ruby Crystals Abrasive Grit: Assorted Abrasive Type: Ruby Country of Origin: Germany Dimension: Assorted Item Length: 100mm Package Size: Set of 5 Stone Shape: Assorted",
