    "name": "CMF-610 Magnetic Finisher - 115V",
    "slug": "cmf-610-magnetic-finisher-115v",
    "description": "Product Description Key Features: Direct-drive, fan-cooled machine for ultra-quiet operation. Auto shutoff function. Clear bowl with fill-line indicators offer easy load preparation of pins and compound Space-saving finisher is fully programmable. Electronic Timer with a digital readout. Compact heavy-duty construction for long life usage. Our CMF-610 magnetic finisher comes complete with a 6\" diameter, heavy-duty plastic, bowl with cover which can accommodate a 30 ring capacity and comes supplied with ample (250 grams) of 0.5mm stainless steel pins as well as Gesswein’s 44S Soap (852-1029) to keep your pins and parts running as clean as possible. Direct-drive, fan-cooled 1/12 HP motor provides variable speed, forward/reverse function to change the direction of media flow and thus not allowing the stainless steel pins to clump in one area of the bowl. 115V, 60Hz. The CMF-610 measures: 10\" x 10\" x 14\" (254 x 254 x 356mm). Shipping weight: 24lbs, Shipping Dimensions: 15\" x 18\" x 15\" (381 x 457 x 381mm) One-Year Warranty. Made in Taiwan These Magnetic Finishers are available in different sizes so one is sure to suit your needs. All are built and engineered to the highest quality standards. Put the power of magnetic finishers to work for you! Magnetic finishing remains today’s state-of-the-art method to finish non-ferrous metals that have a high degree of intricacy with medias (stainless steel pins) as small as 0.30mm in diameter and 0.25mm in length. This method of finishing was first introduced to the jewelry industry with tremendous success for processing precious metals. Magnets embedded in a cast disc constantly change polarity, creating a centrifugal action in the media allowing your finisher to access recesses, channels, undercuts and other confined areas where other conventional methods/medias can't. Soft non-ferrous metals can be burnished in as little as half an hour, ensuring quicker turnaround time and improved productivity. If your pieces have large, smooth or flat surfaces, the finish will appear frosted or have a satin-finish look. A slight buffing or a run in a dry finisher (such as our 852-0746 vibratory tumbler) will easily bring the finish to a high shine. FYI a replacement bowl and cover is also available - our 8520318 Tech Tips : Important! Under no circumstances should the pins be stored in the bowl on the machine. Doing so will cause the pins to magnetize, resulting in over-magnetizing of pins, thus lessening their effectiveness. Note: Other sizes, and 230V models are also available as are replacement bowls. Show More Product Specifications Brand: Misc Country of Origin: Taiwan Dimension: 10\" x 10\" x 14\" Electrical: 115V, 60Hz Model: 115V Pin Capacity: 250g Ring Capacity: 30 Speed Control Type: Variable Speed Warranty Term: 1 Year",
