    "description": "Hammer Kit for setting, engraving, and other jobs requiring a hammering action. See Product Options for North American and 230V Plugs. Use Product Options Menu to Select Plug Option: K.1080 – North American Plug K.1080-21 – United Kingdom Plug CE K.1080-22 – Continental European Plug CE K.1080-26 – Australian Plug Ideal for stone setting applications and engraving techniques that require a hammering action. Hammer can be varied from 0-5,000 strokes per minute. Stone Setting/Engraving Micromotor Kit 1080 includes: 1. H.MH-110 Hammer Handpiece 2. HP4-917 Control Unit (this is the same control unit that comes in Micromotor Kits K.1020, K.1070 and K.1090) 3. H8-214 Graver Holder 4. Accessories described below Two Year Limited Warranty This Hammer Action micromotor is ideal for stone setting applications and engraving techniques. The force of the impact of the H.MH-110 reciprocating handpiece can be adjusted from light to full by turning the metal ring while the motor is off or running. The speed of the hammer action can also be varied from 0-2,500 strokes per minute with the dial on the control unit. Used with the supplied Graver Holder, the handpiece becomes a precision power engraver- no need for an air compressor or a flexible shaft drive. H.MH-110 Reciprocating Handpiece has a slender contoured grip and impact adjustment ring for precise hammering work. Operates from 0-2,500 strokes per minute. Specs- 6-1/4″ overall length, 9/16″ grip diameter, 1″ motor diameter, 13oz/369 gr., 1.5 amps (115V) .75 amps (230V). Screws into the front end of the handpiece and converts it into a power engraving tool. Comes with 5/64″ allen key (graver not included). Accessories in Kit K.1080: Adapter for Threaded Anvil Point (installed) HPH8-32 Anvil Points (3) with Threaded Shanks HP10177 Graver Holder HPH8-214 Screws into the front end of the handpiece and converts it into a power engraving tool. Comes with 5/64″ allen key (graver not included). Graver Holder Screws into front end of H.MH-110 Handpiece and converts it into a power engraving tool. Includes Hex Key and 2 Pins for tightening Anvil Points. Graver not included. K.1080 Hammer Micromotor Owner’s Manual HPMH-110 Micromotor Handpiece Parts List Overview of Foredom’s K.1070, K.1020, K.1080 and K.1090 Micromotor Kits. These “Brush Type” kits utilize the same control box. Video identifies unique and shared kit components. K.1070 – Changing Accessories and Collets K.1070 Micromotor – Changing Motor Brushes K.1070 Micromotor – Changing Fuse Weight 4.3 lbs Dimensions N/A SKU - Power Plug K.1080 – North America, K.1080-21 – United Kingdom, K.1080-22 – Continental Europe, K.1080-26 – Australia",
