    "description": "Replacement Canister Filter for MADC20 Dust Collector. Replacement Canister Filter for Dust Collector The Dust Collector motor has a safety electronic thermal overload prevention circuit which turns the motor off if it gets too hot. This can be caused by both filters being clogged, especially the canister filter MADC208 which is located under the HEPA filter bag. To access the Canister Filter: remove the Top Connector tubing. Then loosen the thumb screws to the filter chamber compartment and twist it until the lid can be removed. You should replace the HEPA filter bag at this time. Then look down into the empty chamber and unscrew the knob screw on the canister filter lid and carefully remove the metal and rubber washers and lid. You can now lift out the canister filter and replace it. Reassemble and start working again. Click on “Downloads” tab for Owner’s Manual with description for changing filters. MADC20 (Domestic 115 Volt) Dust Collector Owner’s Manual MADC20 (International 230 Volt) Dust Collector Owner’s Manual Weight 0.1 lbs Dimensions 10 × 9 × 0.25 in",
